#lecture-page([Crystal structure: the lattice], [9–10], [
  #grid(columns: (43%, 1fr), column-gutter: 8mm,
    [#figure-image("/assets/tridimite_lattice.png", caption: [Crystal lattice: elementary translation vectors.], width: 100%)],
    [
      The periodic structure is defined by an infinite set of points obtained by linear combination of vectors $vec(a)$ and $vec(b)$ — the elementary translations or base vectors:
      #formula($vec(R)_l = vec(R)_(l m) = l vec(a) + m vec(b)$, tag: [(I.1)])
      In Equation (I.1), $vec(R)_l = vec(R)_(l_1 l_2)$ is a crystal translation vector of the lattice, where $l$ and $m$ are the indices of the node. In tensorial notation we have the equivalent definition:
      #formula($vec(R)_l = vec(R)_(l_1 l_2) = l_1 vec(a)_1 + l_2 vec(a)_2$, tag: [(I.2)])
    ]
  )
])

